      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-08-07_WidnesExaminer_art0057" n="art0057">
        <head>ALL-GERMAN METEOR.</head>
        <p>THE ALL-GERMAN METEOR.</p>
        <p>The all-German Meteor scored a notable success in- ths 23 metre class race at Cowes Regatta. The Meteor is manned by Germans, captained by Germans, was designed in Germany, and built in Germany, and her victory seems to suggest that we must now submit to the excellence of Teutonic yachtsmanship. She won, it is true, through the disquali- fication of the Germania, also a German-built boat however. In our illustration the Meteor is showing a clean pair of heels to White Heather and Shamrock.</p>
