        <head>Culcheth.</head>
        <p>Culcheth.</p>
        <p>h aaO4DENT METEIODIST CHAPEL.-1"...e usrml asont Sunday afternoon ws held in this °l,l Sunday last Mr. William Kenyon occupying Solos were very ably rendered by Mrs. vel7.4hurst and Mr. G. Fenton and a recitation was Irnecetsfully given by Mr. Aldred. The childrens ftehal? 1` as also very sweetly rung by some of the lailoa..rs, an address being given afterwards by Mr. R. After the close of the meetirg a collection `aßen in aid of the missionary fund. 'u1t,,,.71NG AT Ctu.CHETH.—A very pretty wedding was 4 t -.140 at the Independent .Blethodisr, aapel on urd •.obt,.. ay lltict by Mr. George Hunter of Leigh. The (iitu;kacting parties were Bliss Susanr au Aldred Avizter of tht stationmaster at Kenyon Junction and !tint.,:lrnes Dunlop of Wigan. The brise who was given 4rid"y her father was attended by her two sisters as ttte toltaids. Mr. W. G. Taylor of Kenycn acted as Iltkutan. The happy couple were the recipients of totet°La presents and later in the day left ft r South- 'there the honeymoon is being spent.</p>
