        <p>LEG WEAKNESS. - Leg weakness is more prevalent in fowls that are high on leg. It is hardly necessary for me to tell you how to know when a bird is suffering from this j . disease. Unable to support the body, they just tumble. about like a drunken man. If therefore you give plety of good food and keep them dry, not much more is needed. Condition powder may be added to the soft food with benefit, Fowls suffering from leg: weakness usually crawl into a quiet spot and get neglected. I have often seen them unable to get under , cover when a storm has been raging. All this 1s detrimental to their recovery, and they should only be. allowed to go into the open run when the weather is favonrable. (To be ronf;n7ted.)</p>
